From: powos-agent <agent@powos>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:24:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: a window that doesn't take a full-screen
 game's focus is held off screen, never in front of it

11-18 21:51 (game-resize 557340, My Friend Pedro; kwin 3.80): the unfold turned "export-new 1" on, and setExportNew
re-exported every window - Steam's main window (empty caption, borderless, no task since the launch) among them. It
didn't take the focus; 0066's 400 ms activation wait ran out while the game's task was "in the background" for the
fold's surface swap, so fullScreenTask() saw no live full-screen task and it opened "as before": a floating task in front
of the game (Steam's store over Bananas in the screenshot, X focus on it, the game never focused, never drew).

1. A full-screen task STANDS while live or within screenSwapGraceMs (3 s) of going to the background (a fold/rotate
   recreates its surface: "in the background", then live again within ~1 s).
2. A new window exported while one stands that did not take the focus (after 0066's wait), is not of a process with a
   task (the game's own dialog: relatedTask, unchanged) and is not full screen itself, is HELD off screen: no task, no
   web window. It opens once it takes the focus (its app brought forward: Steam's raise of its window) or once no
   full-screen task stands (the game closed, left full screen, or out of sight past the grace: the user went home).
   An explicit show (the app's "show <id>": a tap on Steam in the dock/launcher) is not affected.

Decisions in anland_task_policy.h (heldBehindFullScreen, fullScreenTaskStands; test/task-policy-test.cpp).
---
 src/backends/anland/anland_task_policy.h   | 23 +++++++
 src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp | 79 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h   | 11 +++
 3 files changed, 113 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_task_policy.h b/src/backends/anland/anland_task_policy.h
index b2356f3..9828cb3 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_task_policy.h
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_task_policy.h
@@ -25,6 +25,29 @@ inline bool opensOverFullScreen(bool fullScreenTaskShown, bool newWindowActive,
 /** How long a new window may take to get the activation it was started with (an xdg-activation token, an X11 map). */
 constexpr int64_t activationWaitMs = 400;
 
+/**
+ * PowOS (0075): a full-screen task (a game) still stands while it is live, or out of sight only for the moment a fold or
+ * a rotation swaps its surface (the app recreates it: "in the background", then "live" again within ~1 s).
+ */
+constexpr int64_t screenSwapGraceMs = 3000;
+inline bool fullScreenTaskStands(bool live, int64_t msSinceBackground)
+{
+    return live || (msSinceBackground >= 0 && msSinceBackground < screenSwapGraceMs);
+}
+
+/**
+ * PowOS (0075): a window that is exported while a full-screen task stands but did NOT take the focus (after
+ * activationWaitMs) is held off screen - no task, no web window - until it takes the focus (the user brings its app
+ * forward) or no full-screen task stands any more. Opened "as before" (a floating task / a web window that brings home
+ * forward) it went in front of the game: Steam's main window, re-exported when the unfold turned "export-new" on, took
+ * the front over My Friend Pedro (game-resize 557340, 11-18 21:55: the game never focused, never drew). A window of the
+ * game's own process (relatedTask: its dialog) and one going full screen itself (a game of its own) are not held.
+ */
+inline bool heldBehindFullScreen(bool fullScreenTaskStanding, bool newWindowActive, bool relatedToATask, bool newWindowFullScreen)
+{
+    return fullScreenTaskStanding && !newWindowActive && !relatedToATask && !newWindowFullScreen;
+}
+
 enum class RestoreWatch {
     Wait, // nothing to do yet
     Kick, // the restored window has the focus and draws nothing: minimize and restore it again, the way the app sees
